>> title: Smothered Pork Chops
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: pork, gravy, southern, braise, skillet
>> counters: Meat and Three, One Pot
>> aka: smothered chops, pork chops and gravy, smothered pork, chops smothered in onions
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr 20 min
>> slack: narrow — a chop that goes in pale gives a pale gravy, and there is no browning it later once the pan is wet
>> pairs-with: onion-gravy, macaroni-and-cheese, collard-greens, green-beans
>> step.1: Brown the chops hard first and then finish them low in their own gravy. That is what smothered means, and the word runs across chicken, steak, cabbage, potatoes and greens at this counter with the same method behind it every time.
>> step.2: season, both sides
>> step.3: dredge in flour
>> step.4: sear 8 min, both sides
>> step.5: braise covered 45 min

Brown the chops hard first and then finish them low in their own gravy. That is what smothered means, and the word runs across chicken, steak, cabbage, potatoes and greens at this counter with the same method behind it every time.

Season @bone-in pork chops{4}(3/4-in thick, about 2 lb / 900 g) with @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}.

Dredge @&(~1)seasoned chops{} in @all-purpose flour{1/2%cup}(65 g), shaken off.

Sear @&(~1)floured chops{} in @bacon fat{2%Tbs}(28 g) in a #cast-iron skillet{} for ~sear{8%min}, turned once.

Braise @&(~1)seared chops{} covered in @onion gravy{3%cup}(710 mL) for ~braise{45%min}, until a fork goes through the meat.

Spoon what is left in the pan over rice or over mashed potatoes. The gravy is half the order and a plate that comes out dry has been made wrong.
